    <main>
      <section class="demo-hero">
        <div class="wrap">
          <span class="kicker">Comparison demo</span>
          <h1>An animation <em>always plays.</em></h1>
          <p class="sub">Animated mechanisms have no mass and no contact, so nothing ever stops a part. We replay the same parts in physics.</p>
          <nav class="tabs" aria-label="Demo pages">
            <a class="tab" href="../">Datasets in physics</a>
            <a class="tab" href="./" aria-current="page">Animation vs. physics</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="demo-section" aria-label="Animation and physics side by side">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="versus">
            <article class="demo-card versus-row">
              <div class="card-media split" data-sync>
                <figure class="clip"><video data-src="../media/planetary-anim.mp4" data-poster="../media/planetary-anim.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Animated planetary gear turning cleanly"></video><span class="clip-label plain">Animation</span></figure>
                <figure class="clip"><video data-src="../media/planetary-phys.mp4" data-poster="../media/planetary-phys.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="The same planetary gear in physics, with overlapping teeth marked red"></video><span class="clip-label bad">Physics</span></figure>
              </div>
              <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Teeth pass through each other</h3>
                <p>The animation spins the planets on their pins. In physics those pins are locked and the centres sit too close, so the teeth overlap (red).</p>
                <div class="card-meta"><span>Animated toy</span><a class="open-3d" href="../case/?id=planetary"><svg><use href="#i-cube" /></svg>Open in 3D</a></div>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="demo-card versus-row">
              <div class="card-media split" data-sync>
                <figure class="clip"><video data-src="../media/stool-anim.mp4" data-poster="../media/stool-anim.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Animated folding stool closing its X frame"></video><span class="clip-label plain">Animation</span></figure>
                <figure class="clip"><video data-src="../media/stool-phys.mp4" data-poster="../media/stool-phys.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="The same stool in physics stays open under the push"></video><span class="clip-label bad">Physics</span></figure>
              </div>
              <div class="card-body">
                <h3>A stool that cannot fold</h3>
                <p>The animation folds the X frame. In physics each foot is a slider that cannot tilt, so the frame stays open.</p>
                <div class="card-meta"><span>Animated toy</span><a class="open-3d" href="../case/?id=stool"><svg><use href="#i-cube" /></svg>Open in 3D</a></div>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="demo-card versus-row">
              <div class="card-media split" data-sync>
                <figure class="clip"><video data-src="../media/wiper-anim.mp4" data-poster="../media/wiper-anim.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Animated four-bar wiper sweeping"></video><span class="clip-label plain">Animation</span></figure>
                <figure class="clip"><video data-src="../media/wiper-phys.mp4" data-poster="../media/wiper-phys.jpg" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-label="The same wiper in physics: the small push turns the crank and the arm sweeps"></video><span class="clip-label good">Physics</span></figure>
              </div>
              <div class="card-body">
                <h3>Ours: it moves in physics too</h3>
                <p>Under the same small push our wiper sweeps in physics. The arm stops at its designed limit, which the animation swings past.</p>
                <div class="card-meta"><span>FunCAD package</span><a class="open-3d" href="../case/?id=wiperpair"><svg><use href="#i-cube" /></svg>Open in 3D</a></div>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="demo-note">Animated toys are primitive parts moved by closed-form kinematics, the way animation-based methods present mechanisms. Physics runs the same parts with mass and contact under a small push on one joint. Red marks triangles that intersect another part.</p>
          <div class="demo-next"><a class="pill on-page pill-solid" href="../">Datasets in physics<svg><use href="#i-arrow" /></svg></a></div>
